{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace-offering</b> There are many extensions here, to include sin-offering and guilt-offering and the ram of a Nazirite and the festal offering of the fourteenth, that they are eaten for a day and a night — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 7:15). But this is not correct, for the festal offering of the fourteenth is eaten for two days and one night like the rest of peace-offerings, and so we learned in tractate Pesaḥim (Pesaḥim 71a): \"Which you sacrifice in the evening on the first day\" (Deuteronomy 16:4) — Scripture speaks of the festal offering of the fourteenth, which is eaten for two days and one night, for when it says (ibid.) \"on the first day until the morning,\" the second morning is thereby stated. And Rashi himself wrote this in the portion R'eih Anokhi (ibid.). But here the Rav followed the view of Ben Teima (Pesaḥim 70), who said: the festal offering of the fourteenth that comes with the Paschal offering — it is like the Paschal offering and is eaten for a day and a night, and it is eaten only roasted until midnight and is eaten only at night. But according to Ben Teima it is not included in these extensions, but rather it is like the Paschal offering in every respect, and it may come only from the flock, and a male, and in its first year, as it is written (Exodus 34:25) \"and the sacrifice of the feast of the Passover shall not remain until morning,\" and so forth, as is stated there. But the Rav wrote this from the other baraita cited in Torat Kohanim (chapter 12, halakhah 1), which teaches: \"And the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace-offering — on the day of its offering it shall be eaten\" — this comes to teach about those eaten for one day that they are eaten for one day. I have only the thanksgiving offering; from where to include the bread? Scripture says \"its offering.\" And from where to include offspring and substitutions? Scripture says \"and the flesh.\" And from where to include sin-offerings and guilt-offerings? Scripture says \"sacrifice.\" And from where to include the peace-offerings of a Nazirite and peace-offerings that come on account of the Paschal offering? Scripture says \"his peace-offerings.\" This is that baraita, and the Rav explained \"peace-offerings that come on account of the Paschal offering\" as the festal offering of the fourteenth that comes with the Paschal offering. And so I found in tractate Pesaḥim in the chapter Mi Shehaya (96a), where he explained in two expressions \"peace-offerings that come on account of the Paschal offering,\" and in another expression wrote \"the festal offering of the fourteenth\" — this I have heard. And the Rav relied here on his own tradition. But the matter is not so; rather, peace-offerings that come on account of the Paschal offering means the leftover of the Paschal offering, such as its substitution and a Paschal offering whose owners achieved atonement through another, for since at its outset it is eaten only for a day and a night, so too at its conclusion. But the festal offering of the fourteenth is eaten for two days according to the Sages. And so we learned in Torat Kohanim in that very same baraita, which teaches at its end (halakhah 6): \"And on the morrow\" — this comes to teach about those eaten for two days that they are eaten for two days. I have only peace-offerings; from where to include the festal offering that comes in its proper time, and so forth? I include the festal offering that comes in its proper time; from where for the festal offering that comes with the Paschal offering, and so forth?\""], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The Rav refers to Maimonides. The baraita's closing question implies that the festal offering accompanying the Paschal lamb is indeed eaten for two days, contrary to what the Rav inferred from the first part of the baraita."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:33.222323264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}